  "description": "XEHDAR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C77 H70 Dy6 N24 O24,1.5(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.449-4.066 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.31-123.74°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(μ3-OH)3(μ3-CO3)(μ-OMe)(HL)6(MeOH)4(H2O)2]·3MeOH·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
